course: dictionary
lesson: 9558
title: Storyteller
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A storyteller is a person who tells stories, often out loud to an audience. Look at the parts of the word: story plus teller. The teller is the one doing the telling, so a storyteller tells the story.
explain: A storyteller can also be a writer, or someone who is very good at telling stories in an interesting way. «Animal myths travel the same way, from storytellers to cartoon makers.» Here the storytellers are the people who first told these tales, long before the cartoons were drawn.
explain: Storytellers often use words that make the audience feel they are there. «So I'm walking down the road, and this dog comes up to me...» The words I'm and this dog, said out loud, make a past story feel live.
fact: A storyteller is a person who tells stories.
fact: «Storytellers» is the plural: more than one storyteller.
fact: Long ago, storytellers passed on legends and history by speaking them aloud.
fact: Many cultures, including Aboriginal and Maori peoples, have strong storytelling traditions.
fact: Storytellers in different places can tell the same events in their own way.
exercise: What is a storyteller? | A person who sells books in a shop | *A person who tells stories, often out loud | A machine that prints pictures | A person who only reads in silence
exercise: «Storytellers often say "So I'm walking down the road..."» Why do they say it this way? | To tell the time | To say goodbye | *To make a past story feel live | To stop people listening
exercise: Find and copy the plural of storyteller in this sentence: «Animal myths travel the same way, from storytellers to cartoon makers.» | makers | *storytellers | travel | myths
test: Which word means a person who tells stories out loud to an audience? | listener | *storyteller | cartoonist | writer
test: «Long ago, storytellers passed on legends and history by speaking.» What did storytellers pass on? | Shopping lists | Football scores | *Legends and history | Maths tables
exam: «The Bible, the Qur'an and the old books of Ethiopia each tell the visit in their own way.» What does this show about storytellers? | Storytellers always tell exactly the same story | *Different storytellers can tell the same event in their own way | Storytellers only live in Ethiopia | Storytellers never write
